        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity-sec 27a and 27ab",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity-sec 27a and 27ab\n\nThese tests restart every server to check that nodemap data\nsurvives a restart: 27a twice and 27ab twice, each a full module\nreload and remount of every target. That is about 160 seconds on\na 4 VM DNE CI setup, and the tests average 320 to 420 seconds\nin CI.\n\nWhat 27ab checks lives on the MGS, which re-reads the nodemap\nindex from disk when it restarts, and 27a mounts a client\nagainst the fileset the MGS loaded. Restart just the MGS and\nMDT0000, with the clients unmounted, and wait for the other\nMDTs to reconnect to MDT0000. 27a keeps the full restart\nwith module reload when the MGS predates persistent filesets,\nsince an llog fileset is only replayed from the params llog once\nthe in-memory nodemap is freed; 27ac keeps it for the same\nreason, and 27c keeps covering a full restart.\n\nFix 27ac's fileset sync checks, which used undefined variable\nnames and so checked nothing.\n\nOn a 2 MDT, 2 OST, 1 client setup 27a went from 289 s to 93\nto 106 s and 27ab from 166 s to 54 to 63 s: about 300 s per run\nof the two tests, roughly 700 hours per 30 days at 8300 runs of\neach test.\n\nFixes: 40cd140b8597 (\"LU-18357 ptlrpc: Support add and del alternate filesets\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=\"27a 27ab 27ac\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I97e69b2d2211d854bf1b1776246cd665cde51d4e\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70191\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
